Subject: Recover to three previous states for one lookahead token

Recover to more than one previous state for one lookahead token.

The copy of the runtime of the tree-sitter-cpp fork has this repair. The fork commit is
be03945.

Error recovery went back only to the nearest state of the summary that
accepts the lookahead token. That state can be in the construct that has
the error. In `int x = F(typename D::type&&); int y;`, the `;` recovered
into the argument list, and one ERROR held the two declarations.

The recovery now goes back to a maximum of three states that accept the
token, if no better version exists. The error costs then select one of
the versions. GCC and Clang report errors at `&&` and `)` of the argument
list, and the ERROR node now holds only the argument.

On the corpus at e944ebb, the ERROR bytes go from 11.76 MB to 8.22 MB.
The files whose root node is ERROR go from 19 to 1, and the files with an
ERROR over 90% of the file go from 96 to 21. No file without an error
changes. In the benchmark of one error in each of 4,000 files, the named
nodes outside the edit that change go from 17,141 to 14,932 for balanced
brackets, and from 63,964 to 62,316 for unbalanced brackets. With 2, 4,
6, or no limit, the ERROR bytes are more.

The new corpus tests have a member macro with no semicolon before a
directive and before the brace of its class, a type as a function
argument, and a function type as a macro argument.

The repair is not specific to a language. The value 3 comes from a measurement on a corpus of
329,387 C++ files. The values 2, 4, 6, and no limit all give more error bytes.

Risk for upstream: medium. The value is a measurement of one language.

The patch applies to the upstream tag v0.27.0, after the patches with a smaller number. The
series compiles with `-Wall -Wextra` and no warning.

The comments hold the marker "(tree-sitter-cpp fork)". Remove the marker before you send the
patch upstream.

diff -ruN a/lib/src/parser.c b/lib/src/parser.c
--- a/lib/src/parser.c	2026-09-15 19:00:45.713775622 +0200
+++ b/lib/src/parser.c	2026-09-15 19:00:45.728015329 +0200
@@ -80,6 +80,12 @@
 // 16, a C++ file with an error in a deep construct cannot get back to the translation unit at the end
 // of the file, and its root node is ERROR (tree-sitter-cpp fork).
 static const unsigned MAX_SUMMARY_DEPTH = 256;
+// The number of previous states that error recovery goes back to for one lookahead token. The
+// published runtime goes back only to the nearest state that accepts the token. That state can be
+// in the construct that has the error, and a later error then makes a large ERROR node. With more
+// versions, the error costs select the state. On the C++ corpus, 3 gives fewer ERROR bytes than
+// 2, 4, 6, or no limit (tree-sitter-cpp fork).
+static const unsigned MAX_RECOVERY_COUNT = 3;
 static const unsigned MAX_COST_DIFFERENCE = 18 * ERROR_COST_PER_SKIPPED_TREE;
 static const unsigned OP_COUNT_PER_PARSER_CALLBACK_CHECK = 100;
 
@@ -1296,6 +1302,7 @@
   Subtree lookahead
 ) {
   bool did_recover = false;
+  unsigned recovery_count = 0;
   unsigned previous_version_count = ts_stack_version_count(self->stack);
   Length position = ts_stack_position(self->stack, version);
   StackSummary *summary = ts_stack_get_summary(self->stack, version);
@@ -1355,13 +1362,14 @@
       if (ts_parser__better_version_exists(self, version, false, new_cost)) break;
 
       // If the current lookahead token is valid in some previous state, recover to that state.
-      // Then stop looking for further recoveries.
+      // Stop after MAX_RECOVERY_COUNT recoveries.
       if (ts_language_has_actions(self->language, entry.state, ts_subtree_symbol(lookahead))) {
         if (ts_parser__recover_to_state(self, version, depth, entry.state)) {
           did_recover = true;
+          recovery_count++;
           LOG("recover_to_previous state:%u, depth:%u", entry.state, depth);
           LOG_STACK();
-          break;
+          if (recovery_count == MAX_RECOVERY_COUNT) break;
         }
       }
     }
